    "answer": {
      "short": "$14\\sqrt3\\text{ cm}^2$",
      "worked": "Let $\\theta=\\angle ACB$. Use the cosine rule to find the included angle.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{8^2+7^2-13^2}{2(8)(7)}\\\\\n\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac12\\\\\n\\theta&=120^\\circ\n\\end{align*}$$\nThen use the area rule.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Area}&=\\frac12(8)(7)\\sin120^\\circ\\\\\n\\text{Area}&=14\\sqrt3\\text{ cm}^2\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
